{% comment %}
  Renders a dynamic "price per sq ft" line for flooring products.

  The figure is computed at render time from the CURRENT variant price and the
  product's coverage area, so it never goes stale when pricing changes — there
  are no hardcoded price-per-sq-ft values to maintain.

  Coverage is derived from the existing length_in x width_in dimension
  metafields (inches -> sq ft), e.g. 984 in x 78 in / 144 = approx. 533 sq ft.

  Scoped to flooring via the custom.main_category metafield so it never shows
  on non-flooring products (treadmills, racks, etc. also carry length/width).

  Renders nothing unless the product is flooring AND has usable dimensions AND
  a price. On combined listings the value is updated per selected grade by the
  variant-change JS in main-product-comb.liquid (see [data-price-per-sqft]).

  Accepts:
  - product: {Object} Product Liquid object (required)
{% endcomment %}
{%- liquid
  assign category = product.metafields.custom.main_category | downcase | strip
  assign length_in = product.metafields.custom.length_in | times: 1.0
  assign width_in = product.metafields.custom.width_in | times: 1.0
  assign variant = product.selected_or_first_available_variant
  assign coverage_sqft = 0
  if length_in > 0 and width_in > 0
    assign coverage_sqft = length_in | times: width_in | divided_by: 144.0
  endif
-%}
{%- if category == 'flooring' and coverage_sqft > 0 and variant.price > 0 -%}
  {%- assign price_per_sqft = variant.price | divided_by: coverage_sqft | round -%}
  <div class="price-per-sqft" data-price-per-sqft-wrap data-coverage-sqft="{{ coverage_sqft | round }}">
    approx. <span data-price-per-sqft>{{ price_per_sqft | money }}</span> per sq ft
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
